{"title":"1978 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 20th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1978 in Romania.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cdf676c3182b84e9a863fbf223c1abe492715f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le m &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. In their decimal representations, the last three digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d655eb08535de0b94232fd4973aa70f434edbd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are equal, respectively, to the last three digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be958d0ced3fbfac442fe97c2a8a48616bc4e6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> has its least value.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We consider a fixed point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the interior of a fixed sphere<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52dd46b7fc4df2f724b5af4311a675147cd6e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.$\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> We construct three segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc5743b064a8f8d0b1639842ca8f5cc43d4e65c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA, PB,PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />, perpendicular two by two<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d198e115ee5481f6012df3f623690b4bcab5f869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"4\" height=\"5\" /> with the vertexes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> on the sphere<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52dd46b7fc4df2f724b5af4311a675147cd6e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.$\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> We consider the vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> which is opposite to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the parallelepiped (with right angles) with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc695bddd2dfe513231641c91d1afb3c8708a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA, PB, PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> as edges<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52dd46b7fc4df2f724b5af4311a675147cd6e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.$\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> Find the locus of the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> take all the positions compatible with our problem.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d2f190d69190e2547283f5787d26da1ef8d7ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;f(1)&lt;f(2)&lt;f(3)&lt;\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" /> a sequence with all its terms positive<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52dd46b7fc4df2f724b5af4311a675147cd6e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.$\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f0b29305e947b3755e0703980ff2aa077e72d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> positive integer which doesn't belong to the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f18f0a21db321804f4034d2e91765d5acdd5e8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(n))+1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170e0bc0141f541dfe499294be61f197951b3de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(240).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/33901614db4565ea5dfabf01b3c25e3c9673e97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC.$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> A circle which is internally tangent with the circumscribed circle of the triangle is also tangent to the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547f225d9af24dda08195ad51ee009872c3d3fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> in the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede78a06018011f48c24a76284afce482ebc6c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> respectively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b727b773d199f4fa0d684957a720f9c3e9750c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> Prove that the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the center of the inscribed circle of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd222166def59a3315433877917a826de6488031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be an injective function from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06cc90a55154119e08022c416832b4981fe19975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,2,3,\\ldots}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> in itself. Prove that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb4ec92fd3acf0b7b5eb976ace404d2e070f419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{n} f(k)k^{-2} \\geq \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k^{-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"176\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>An international society has its members from six different countries. The list of members contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967eac36d2d8bbd6ff14f1c5e40d154d4a7e93d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> names, numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/2684c226b310bd1261b68ec4fbf5026e4fbb08e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\dots, 1978$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that there is at least one member whose number is the sum of the numbers of two members from his own country, or twice as large as the number of one member from his own country.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO\" title=\"1978 IMO\">1978 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1978\">IMO 1978 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO\" title=\"1978 IMO\">1978 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO\" title=\"1977 IMO\">1977 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO\" title=\"1979 IMO\">1979 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018042516\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 237/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6544/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.350      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.350      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17877:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018042516 and revision id 143960. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}